1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire
Knight of the Ribbon

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Knight of the Ribbon,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,107 --> 00:01:50,147
Forty-Second Episode
The Rat Man
The Great Rat Removal Strategy

15
00:02:09,024 --> 00:02:10,577
Here's to good health and good fortune, my friend!

16
00:02:10,602 --> 00:02:13,037
What a glorious day! What a glorious day!

17
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:33,900
Wow, so pretty!

18
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:34,746
Yes.

19
00:02:36,289 --> 00:02:38,453
I'm going too!

20
00:02:39,909 --> 00:02:41,360
Wait for me. I'm coming too.

21
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:43,886
Well, not dressed like that.

22
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:46,146
Please wait for me then.

23
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,446
You're terrible, Sapphire!

24
00:02:54,471 --> 00:02:55,500
Sorry to keep you waiting.

25
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:57,806
Let's hurry.

26
00:03:04,724 --> 00:03:07,257
Long live Silverland!

27
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:20,160
A bumper crop! A bumper crop!

28
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,953
Come on, drink up! Drink up!

29
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,360
Why, look at that! We've got a bumper crop of rats this year, too!

30
00:03:42,213 --> 00:03:44,213
Help me!

31
00:04:06,350 --> 00:04:11,340
My dear rats, Silverland's storehouse is full of delicious wheat.

32
00:04:12,475 --> 00:04:14,033
Go quickly and eat up.

33
00:04:44,699 --> 00:04:47,333
Where on earth did so many rats come from?

34
00:04:55,001 --> 00:04:56,760
This has turned into a disaster...

35
00:04:56,860 --> 00:04:57,860
What should we do?

36
00:04:58,320 --> 00:04:59,619
We're in real trouble...

37
00:05:02,246 --> 00:05:09,420
It's over. There's nothing left to eat in this kingdom until the next harvest.

38
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:12,640
Forget that! At this rate, we won't even have food on the table today!

39
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:18,173
At this rate, we're all going to starve to death!

40
00:05:26,615 --> 00:05:30,060
Lord Duralumin, did you happen to see the commotion in the village last night?

41
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:32,740
Well, they certainly went on quite a wild rampage.

42
00:05:33,053 --> 00:05:38,726
Still, I'd expect no less from the Rat Man sent by Lord X.

43
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,480
What incredible power!

44
00:05:41,455 --> 00:05:46,862
If Lord X's army invades next month, this kingdom won't stand a chance.

45
00:05:46,886 --> 00:05:49,140
Starving soldiers won't even have the energy to run away.

46
00:05:55,490 --> 00:05:59,973
I am an envoy from Goldland. I bring a letter for the King of Silverland.

47
00:06:00,695 --> 00:06:02,720
What? From Goldland?

48
00:06:11,590 --> 00:06:13,009
<i>Hear me, everyone!</i>

49
00:06:13,033 --> 00:06:16,615
<i>The King of neighboring Goldland, moved by our recent disaster, </i>

50
00:06:16,639 --> 00:06:18,586
<i>has agreed to lend us wheat.</i>

51
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:25,928
<i>His Majesty urges all citizens to rest assured and rise above this tragedy.</i>

52
00:06:25,953 --> 00:06:26,526
<i>That is all!</i>

53
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:31,935
That's great! That's great!

54
00:06:31,959 --> 00:06:34,306
Let's make the granary sturdier!

55
00:06:46,330 --> 00:06:48,806
Let's see... What are we missing...

56
00:06:51,235 --> 00:06:52,653
I'll tell you right now!

57
00:06:56,780 --> 00:06:58,980
Heavenly Father, forgive me!

58
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,139
But I'm too hungry to sleep!

59
00:07:03,106 --> 00:07:06,333
Living as a human is so inconvenient!

60
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:13,520
Duralumin and Nylon.

61
00:07:13,895 --> 00:07:15,286
Where are they going now?

62
00:07:16,653 --> 00:07:17,653
All right!

63
00:07:40,466 --> 00:07:41,400
Pardon the intrusion!

64
00:07:43,670 --> 00:07:45,289
Well, well... what a fine gathering!

65
00:07:46,899 --> 00:07:48,560
Oh? Interrupting your meal, are we?

66
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:52,382
How about joining me?

67
00:07:53,239 --> 00:07:54,373
Well, don't mind if I do.

68
00:07:56,830 --> 00:07:59,122
This smells great. What is it?

69
00:07:59,146 --> 00:08:02,280
It's a stewed mixture of earthworms, caterpillars, and spiders.

70
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:05,880
What about this delicious-looking fried dish?

71
00:08:06,826 --> 00:08:08,186
Oh no, that's a toad.

72
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,620
Then how about centipede soup?

73
00:08:11,621 --> 00:08:13,260
No, I'll pass.

74
00:08:13,750 --> 00:08:15,980
Looks like none of it is to your liking.

75
00:08:16,610 --> 00:08:17,920
How about a drink, then?

76
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:20,893
If it's booze...

77
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:21,980
I'll gladly take some.

78
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:25,980
Delicious! This hits the spot!

79
00:08:26,055 --> 00:08:27,055
All right!

80
00:08:27,405 --> 00:08:29,640
Newt wine really builds up your strength, after all.

81
00:08:34,814 --> 00:08:37,400
Hey, hey, I'm trying to eat here!

82
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:39,562
Pardon me.

83
00:08:39,586 --> 00:08:42,589
We went through all that trouble using your power

84
00:08:42,613 --> 00:08:46,080
to wipe out the wheat, but that meddling King of Goldland...

85
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,962
Don't worry.

86
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:52,260
Not a single grain of wheat will reach them from Goldland.

87
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:55,349
So on their way...?

88
00:08:55,373 --> 00:09:00,220
Exactly. It's about time I fed my lovely rats.

89
00:09:05,029 --> 00:09:07,220
There, there. Good work coming all this way.

90
00:09:11,739 --> 00:09:14,462
The wheat supply convoy will depart

91
00:09:14,486 --> 00:09:17,480
tomorrow morning under Prince Franz of Goldland's command.

92
00:09:20,469 --> 00:09:22,846
So, where will you crush them?

93
00:09:23,389 --> 00:09:26,729
First, after leaving Goldland, the convoy will stay here,

94
00:09:26,753 --> 00:09:29,320
and camp around this area the next night.

95
00:09:29,494 --> 00:09:33,629
We'll ambush them by this river and let the rats eat every last grain.

96
00:09:33,653 --> 00:09:37,386
But aren't there both eastern and western roads from Goldland?

97
00:09:38,099 --> 00:09:41,180
No, they are sure to take this western road.

98
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:43,755
The eastern road is a steep mountain path,

99
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:46,859
making it hard for wagons loaded with wheat to pass.

100
00:09:47,020 --> 00:09:50,700
Even if it's a detour, they'll undoubtedly take the flat western road.

101
00:09:51,646 --> 00:09:52,946
I see.

102
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:58,540
You truly live up to your reputation as Lord X's right-hand man, Lord Rat.

103
00:10:07,249 --> 00:10:09,340
Oh no, I'm scared!

104
00:10:14,634 --> 00:10:18,020
Hey, we have a guests! Quiet down, will you?

105
00:10:27,419 --> 00:10:28,060
Is that true?

106
00:10:28,430 --> 00:10:30,940
That's right. If we don't hurry, something terrible will happen.

107
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:31,860
All right!

108
00:10:39,519 --> 00:10:41,566
Sapphire! Hurry!

109
00:10:41,775 --> 00:10:42,400
Okay!

110
00:10:46,985 --> 00:10:49,666
Sapphire! Take me too!

111
00:10:50,849 --> 00:10:53,506
She gets so carried away whenever it comes to seeing Franz.

112
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:14,091
Come out, my rats! Come out and follow me!

113
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:18,186
I'll feed you plenty of delicious Goldland wheat!

114
00:11:19,650 --> 00:11:20,650
Go!

115
00:11:45,019 --> 00:11:47,160
Prince Franz, are you ready?

116
00:11:48,345 --> 00:11:52,660
All right, no matter what happens, we'll deliver this wheat to Silverland!

117
00:11:54,346 --> 00:11:55,460
Move out!

118
00:12:20,959 --> 00:12:21,853
We're too slow!

119
00:12:23,299 --> 00:12:24,299
Come on, keep pushing!

120
00:12:25,419 --> 00:12:27,540
Though we've still got quite a journey ahead of us...

121
00:12:52,609 --> 00:12:54,820
Franz! I'm glad I made it in time!

122
00:12:58,949 --> 00:13:00,939
Ribbon Knight! What are you doing here?

123
00:13:02,130 --> 00:13:04,140
Lord Sapphire sent this to you...

124
00:13:06,239 --> 00:13:06,944
Sapphire...

125
00:13:11,042 --> 00:13:11,740
What? An ambush?

126
00:13:12,946 --> 00:13:15,158
Prince Franz, this is our chance!

127
00:13:15,342 --> 00:13:18,179
Let's set a trap instead and wipe out those rats!

128
00:13:18,545 --> 00:13:19,431
Alright, let's do it!

129
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:50,080
All set. Now we just wait for tomorrow.

130
00:14:18,934 --> 00:14:20,701
Hurry! Night will fall before we know it!

131
00:14:24,924 --> 00:14:27,786
Tonight, I'll teach them a lesson!

132
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:54,506
Now, my lovely rats, go feast on the wheat in that wagon.

133
00:15:03,409 --> 00:15:05,080
The rats are acting strange.

134
00:15:09,060 --> 00:15:10,060
It's a doll!

135
00:15:14,549 --> 00:15:16,220
Oh, this is gunpowder.

136
00:15:16,855 --> 00:15:18,753
And oil... Oh no!

137
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:20,940
Damn it!

138
00:15:24,696 --> 00:15:26,140
Now! Take that!

139
00:15:43,413 --> 00:15:45,300
My rats!

140
00:15:45,701 --> 00:15:46,947
Damn it!

141
00:15:55,489 --> 00:15:56,540
Over here! This way!

142
00:15:57,355 --> 00:15:58,740
Come to me, everyone!

143
00:16:00,775 --> 00:16:03,640
You poor things, forgive me!

144
00:16:03,820 --> 00:16:05,699
I let my guard down!

145
00:16:12,913 --> 00:16:14,893
Cut the ropes!

146
00:16:29,420 --> 00:16:33,706
Mark my words, Franz! I will have my revenge for this!

147
00:16:57,827 --> 00:16:58,587
It's close.

148
00:17:05,149 --> 00:17:06,383
Just as I thought!

149
00:17:07,141 --> 00:17:08,726
This dangerous pass is the exact spot they'd attack!

150
00:17:30,809 --> 00:17:32,783
Landslide! Halt!

151
00:17:41,444 --> 00:17:43,760
Curse that Ribbon Knight! Just you wait!

152
00:17:49,439 --> 00:17:51,199
Ha! A hit! It hit!

153
00:17:51,284 --> 00:17:54,646
Charge! Finish them off! Get them!

154
00:17:58,340 --> 00:17:59,340
Fire!

155
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:01,893
Hey, wait!

156
00:18:02,519 --> 00:18:04,340
Are you alright, Ribbon Knight?

157
00:18:05,313 --> 00:18:06,000
I'm fine!

158
00:18:07,004 --> 00:18:08,905
Thank you for saving me back there...

159
00:18:09,283 --> 00:18:11,760
No, no, you've saved me so many times yourself...

160
00:18:13,356 --> 00:18:14,193
What about that wound?

161
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:15,039
It's nothing...

162
00:18:15,456 --> 00:18:16,860
I'll have my men tend to it right away.

163
00:18:17,624 --> 00:18:20,500
No, I'm really fine. See you later!

164
00:18:21,853 --> 00:18:22,779
Ribbon Knight!

165
00:18:26,189 --> 00:18:27,320
What a strange fellow...

166
00:18:55,153 --> 00:18:56,281
Loves me...

167
00:18:56,619 --> 00:18:57,660
Loves me not...

168
00:18:59,159 --> 00:18:59,645
Loves me...

169
00:19:04,849 --> 00:19:05,886
Y-You're...!

170
00:19:08,290 --> 00:19:09,290
I'm sorry I'm late.

171
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:13,300
How did you get that wound?

172
00:19:15,566 --> 00:19:19,512
I was just careless with a rose thorn in the garden...

173
00:19:20,203 --> 00:19:22,679
Any rose that dares hurt your beautiful hand,

174
00:19:22,703 --> 00:19:25,280
I'd slice to pieces with this sword!

175
00:19:26,064 --> 00:19:26,786
How sweet...

176
00:19:51,944 --> 00:19:53,171


177
00:19:57,829 --> 00:19:59,173
Sapphire, the sword!

178
00:19:59,500 --> 00:19:59,913
Yes!

179
00:20:29,303 --> 00:20:30,300
Now's the time!

180
00:20:32,836 --> 00:20:34,100
Now stay still!

181
00:20:36,619 --> 00:20:38,093
Who are you?

182
00:20:38,118 --> 00:20:39,447
Why are you attacking us?

183
00:20:39,472 --> 00:20:41,386
Start talking!

184
00:20:42,859 --> 00:20:47,240
This is revenge for the rats you wiped out!

185
00:20:47,715 --> 00:20:48,715
Rats?

186
00:20:52,359 --> 00:20:55,640
Sorry to interrupt, but would you mind letting that rat man go?

187
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:57,774
What are you saying, Lord Nylon?!

188
00:20:58,431 --> 00:21:00,853
So you teamed up with this man to...

189
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:03,047
That's right.

190
00:21:03,071 --> 00:21:06,946
The plan was to use the rats to ravage the kingdom,

191
00:21:06,971 --> 00:21:08,900
then take it over.

192
00:21:14,746 --> 00:21:15,893
Hey, where are you going?

193
00:21:16,559 --> 00:21:19,387
Now that the plan has failed, I'm no longer needed here.

194
00:21:19,411 --> 00:21:21,780
I'll just go back and report to Lord X.

195
00:21:22,429 --> 00:21:23,886
Th-That's impossible!

196
00:21:23,985 --> 00:21:24,985
See ya!

197
00:21:25,514 --> 00:21:27,286
W-Wait!

198
00:21:33,280 --> 00:21:34,940
Sorry to bother you.

199
00:21:44,669 --> 00:21:45,460
Franz

200
00:21:46,171 --> 00:21:46,987
Franz

201
00:21:47,011 --> 00:21:49,713
That's enough. Why don't you forgive him now?

202
00:21:51,213 --> 00:21:52,720
What a hopeless bunch.

203
00:21:52,744 --> 00:21:53,840
Still, I'm glad it's over.

204
00:21:53,864 --> 00:21:57,373
They were a formidable enemy, but this should teach the X-Union a lesson.

205
00:22:37,909 --> 00:22:44,420
I think they'd look great together if they got along like those dolls.

206
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:25,000
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

207
00:23:25,001 --> 00:23:28,361
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

208
00:23:28,362 --> 00:23:32,132
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

209
00:23:32,133 --> 00:23:35,294
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

210
00:23:35,295 --> 00:23:39,108
♪ Sen'nen man'nen hyakuman-nen ♪
A thousand years, ten thousand years, a million years,

211
00:23:39,109 --> 00:23:42,405
♪ Ribbon de tsunagou ichioku-nen ♪
Let’s connect with ribbons for a billion years!

212
00:23:42,406 --> 00:23:46,411
♪ Akuma ga kute mo arashi ga kute mo ♪
Even if demons come, even if storms arrive,

213
00:23:46,412 --> 00:23:49,850
♪ tsunaida kokoro wa hanarenai ♪
Our bonded hearts will never part.

214
00:23:49,851 --> 00:23:53,471
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

215
00:23:53,472 --> 00:23:56,832
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

216
00:23:56,833 --> 00:24:00,603
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

217
